              "question": "<p>Common side effects associated with pseudoephedrine therapy include central nervous system stimulation, insomnia, nervousness, excitability, dizziness and anxiety. To offset this, the night time version of cold and flu medications including pseudoephedrine often include a first generation antihistamine, as those make a person feel drowsy.</p>\n"
